<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cattaraugus Reservation</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cattaraugus Reservation is a territory of the Seneca Nation of Indians along Cattaraugus <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>, near Lake Erie in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. It was one of the lands kept by the Seneca after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-big-tree">Treaty of Big Tree</a> in 1797. In 1848 its people joined those of Allegany to form the Seneca Nation's elected republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cattaraugus-reservation.jpg" alt="Cattaraugus Reservation" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: awmcphee · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:0540R_Cattaraugus_Reservation_Locator_Map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
